<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept id="expand_complex_types">

 <title>EXPAND_COMPLEX_TYPES Query Option</title>
 <titlealts audience="PDF"><navtitle>EXPAND COMPLEX TYPES</navtitle></titlealts>
 <prolog>
  <metadata>
   <data name="Category" value="Impala"/>
   <data name="Category" value="Impala Query Options"/>
   <data name="Category" value="Troubleshooting"/>
   <data name="Category" value="Querying"/>
   <data name="Category" value="Developers"/>
   <data name="Category" value="Data Analysts"/>
  </metadata>
 </prolog>

 <conbody>
  <p>
   <indexterm audience="hidden">EXPAND_COMPLEX_TYPES Query Option</indexterm> Older versions of
   Impala did not support complex types in the select list, and therefore a <codeph>SELECT
   *</codeph> statement only expanded to primitive types even when the table contained complex-typed
   columns. Support for complex types in the select list has since been added, and <q>*</q>
   expressions now include complex types by default. If the EXPAND_COMPLEX_TYPES query option is set
   to false, <q>*</q> expressions skip complex types, restoring the behaviour of earlier Impala
   versions.
  </p>

  <p>
   Note: even if EXPAND_COMPLEX_TYPES is false, complex-typed columns that are listed explicitly in
   the select list (i.e. not as a <q>*</q> expression) will be included in the result.
  </p>

  <p conref="../shared/impala_common.xml#common/type_boolean"/>
  <p conref="../shared/impala_common.xml#common/default_true_1"/>
  <note>
   The default value was changed to <codeph>true</codeph> starting from
   <keyword keyref="impala50"/>. In earlier releases the default was <codeph>false</codeph>.
   For the statements that this change affects, see
   <xref href="impala_incompatible_changes.xml#incompatible_changes_500x"/>.
  </note>
  <p><b>Added in:</b> <keyword keyref="impala42"/></p>
  <p conref="../shared/impala_common.xml#common/related_info"/>
  <p>
   <xref href="impala_complex_types.xml"/>,
   <xref href="impala_incompatible_changes.xml#incompatible_changes_500x"/>
  </p>
 </conbody>
</concept>
